<!--/Post: 13285-->
<!--Post: 13288--><!--Time: 1114810050-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13288"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Affie4u<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Affie4u<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 29, 2005 - 2:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->That must cost a lot of money to be boarding that dog each day. <BR> <BR>If a family memeber like BTK wife or daughter does not want to pick the dog up because they are afraid to come to park city &#40;they probley do not want a picture of them being taken &#41;you would think that a family friend or somebody from there church can pick the dog up from the vet and meet them somewhere to give them the dog back. <BR> <BR>Just think of all the &#34;secerts&#34; that dog probley knows . If olny he could talk...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13288-->
<!--Post: 13300--><!--Time: 1114838891-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13300"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsbarn<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsbarn<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 29, 2005 - 10:28 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->But the children can talk. <BR> <BR>Someone caring in Wichita go adopt that dog! <!--/Text--></td></tr>
